<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chakhundorj</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1699">1699</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Chikhundorj</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chakhundorj was Tüsheet Khan, ruler of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalkha-mongols">Khalkha</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, from 1655 to 1699, and the elder brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanabazar">Zanabazar</a>. His war with the western Khalkha <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zasagt-khan">Zasagt Khan</a> in 1687, in which the Zasagt Khan was killed, gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> ruler Galdan a pretext to invade Khalkha in 1688. Defeated, Chakhundorj and Zanabazar led their people south to seek Qing protection, and in 1691 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dolon-nor">Dolon Nor</a> the Khalkha princes submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangxi-emperor">Kangxi Emperor</a>.</p></div>
